    "title": "Harrison high School installs new turf field - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) — One Evansville high school will have a new playing surface for its football team starting this fall.\nHarrison High School got a new turf field installed. The new surface replaces the old turf which one school official says was showing signs of age.\nHarrison’s athletic director tells us having a field added to the facility they have will make a big difference to those who get to use it. The first football game on the new field will take place September 4 as the Harrison Warriors host the North Huskies.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "(WEHT) — One Evansville high school will have a new playing surface for its football team starting this fall. Harrison High School got a new turf field installed. The new surface replaces the old turf which one school official says was showing signs of age. Harrison’s athletic director tells us having a field added to the facility they have will make a big difference to those who get to use it. The first football game on the new field will take place September 4 as the Harrison Warriors host the North Huskies.",
